/-!
# Permutation data for the degree-four natural-dual actors

The three marked E₁₆ subgroups exhaust the conjugacy classes in Aut(GL₄(2)),
with unique class indices and actual conjugating elements. Their eight-point
orbit partitions are 4², 2⁴ and 2²·4. The two outer-involution classes have
inner centralizers S₆ and C₂ × S₄, given by multiplicative equivalences.

The specified tree Sylow has A₀ as the unique elementary subgroup of largest
order in its inner intersection. The Chapter H adapter applies the source's
elementary Thompson definition to this intrinsic uniqueness result.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), H.9.3(1,3),
printed pp.391–392, PDF pp.402–403.
-/
